anv: AV1 HuC BRC models a GOP with one B frame between the anchors, as media-driver

media-driver (Av1Brc::SetDmemForInit / SetDmemForUpdate) gives the BRC kernel a GOP of GopRefDist > 1 as
INIT_GopP/GopB/GopB1/GopB2, UPD_MaxBRCLevel from GopRefDist and types random access inter frames as B when the
application sends no hierarchy level. ANV described every GOP as all P frames. With Vulkan's flat reference pattern
only GopRefDist 2 has a consistent split (P = B = intra period / 2); 3 gives media-driver a negative GopB2 and 4 or 8
count B1/B2 frames that a flat GOP does not have, so those keep the all-P model.
Goes with 0047 (two PAK passes, which bring the overshoot of this model from 27/19/9% to 18/14/9%) and an encoder
that asks for one B frame. 1080p60 VBR 3/6/12 Mbit/s, 1 B frame, with 0047, BD-rate against SVT-AV1 (PSNR-Y / VMAF):
Netflix Aerial +156.7% / +84.4% (all-P model) -> +135.7% / +68.6%, DrivingPOV +133.9% / +79.8% -> +108.0% / +61.9%.

